# Emulation scratch: `adapter-k8s emulate` copies these out of the (ignored)
# .k8s-adapter/ build output on every run and always overwrites them, so the
# contents are pure generated output — tracking them only churned a regenerated
# build id into every diff. No code reads them; the dir is recreated as needed.
fixtures/*/config/

# Review finding #58: the pool-server suites mkdtemp their staged apps INSIDE the repo root
# (createRequire(<staged>/package.json) has to resolve the repo's `next`), so an interrupted
# run leaves them behind — and the e2e harness packs the adapter from the working tree, which
# means leftovers can ride into a deploy.
.smoke-stage-*/
.headers-stage-*/
.harden-stage-*/
.image-stage-*/
.image-admit-stage-*/
.instr-stage-*/
.draft-stage-*/
